From 39f30fcc26b98e62d4f8f32480b9a49769aac70f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:35:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/adc: MCP3204 SPI ADC and the Thumbstick Click

- mchp-mcp3204: MCP3204 data sheet (DS21298) bit by bit: start bit,
  SGL/DIFF and channel, sample clock, null bit, 12 bits MSB first, then
  LSB first while CS stays low; CS high ends it; single-ended and
  differential pairs; "in0".."in3" and "vref" in mV.
- click-thumbstick: an MCP3204 with the joystick on CH0 (vertical, more
  is down) and CH1 (horizontal, more is right), as MikroElektronika's
  driver reads it; "x", "y" (-1000..1000) and "pressed"; the switch is a
  GPIO output (0 pressed, -1 released).
- mikrobus: "thumbstick" (schematic v101): switch on INT with R3 10k
  pull-up, CS# R2 100k pull-up.
- qtests: centre, axes, differential, unconnected channels, another
  byte alignment with the LSB-first tail, the switch; on mikroBUS 3 of
  the Nano Base too.

Not checked against a physical Thumbstick Click.

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted, not for upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
